 now let's touch on  battery life since you may have heard  that 5g drains your battery faster  and it's true apple does have a new  smart data mode to give you the best mix  of performance and battery life  but if you want you can manually switch  to lte since  it's already so fast the iphone 12's  battery life isn't  amazing but it's much better than most  iphones  mr who's the boss does killer battery  life tests and the new 12 beat out the  11 by about an hour and a half  and the previous 10r by over two hours  the crazy thing is that the iphone 10r  was known for its great battery life  so if you have an older iphone the  difference will be huge  an iphone 12 will get most people  through a full day without needing to  top off  a big part of this is the new a14  processor which is the first five  nanometer processor on the market  that's a big deal because of its battery  efficiency and its crazy fast speeds  everything is super smooth and fast to  be honest  it is way too fast to even use it all  and almost no app can make full use of  all this extra performance that's  exactly what you want though  because it means that three years from  now it will still handle  every new app coming out without a  problem and if you keep it for five  years  you'll still have a usable iphone if you  play mobile games the iphone 12  is great for a few reasons first it can  play every game out there at the best  graphics settings  and likely will be able to do that for  the next couple years  second the display looks fantastic but  more on this in just a bit  and third the speakers which sound great  for games and videos  the speakers are louder and richer than  ever but if you're somebody with an  iphone that's a few years old  the difference is incredible we have  stereo sound from the bottom and the  earpiece speakers  and comparing it to an iphone 8 or 10  it's now  perfectly balanced and compared to an  iphone 7 or older  the stereo sound is much more immersive  making movie watching  actually enjoyable now let's jump to the  screen and apple has  finally perfected it for the first time  an only display is used in a non  thousand dollar iphone which means that  blacks are perfectly black  and you can watch hdr video where colors  and brightness really pop  last year's iphone 11 had a cheap lcd  which wasn't very sharp  and it dimmed if you viewed it from the  side and the 11 pro had an oled screen  that looked blue from the side  but this year fixes both of those issues  and it looks great  now let's get to the first issue that  you might not have with your older  iphone  and that is how easily the screen  scratches  in the last few years apple has been  making the glass tougher against cracks  and this year they are using crystals  which they call ceramic shield  which with the new design makes it four  times stronger against drops the issue  that comes up is that when glass  is tougher against cracks it is easier  to scratch  and even though i've been super careful  with it i've already noticed a few of  them  if this bugs you like it does me i would  suggest getting a glass screen protector  which i'll link down in the video  description  along with a few cases now for those of  you that don't use  cases or screen protectors cracks will  be much less of an issue than before  a big part of this is the old but new  design  straight out of 2010. to be honest i  wasn't super hyped about it like vadim  was  but as soon as i got it in my hand i  fell in love the square edges do make  the phone feel thicker  even though it's actually much thinner  than an iphone 11 but because of that it  feels so much more secure in the hand  the back is all glossy glass and it's  also  much more grippy compared to older  aluminum iphones  but it's definitely a fingerprint magnet  especially with darker colors  speaking of magnets the iphone 12 has a  bunch of them  inside to support max save charging and  a bunch of upcoming accessories  now i don't think this is a big deal yet  but in the future it definitely will be  now what is a big deal is the  waterproofing  this thing can stay 20 feet under water  for 30 minutes which is a huge upgrade  to the older iphones  and makes water a non-issue the bezels  are much thinner now and if you're  coming from an older iphone the screen  fills up the full front as well  which makes it more expansive while  keeping the phone small  because of this if you're somebody that  has an older plus model for the larger  screen  but you find it uncomfortable a regular  iphone 12  should be a very nice middle ground now  let's talk about that notch  and face id yes it does get in the way  sometimes if you watch videos in full  screen and it can cut into some games  and yes you do get used to it overall  it's mostly worth the trade-off in order  to have face id i say mostly  because in 2020 many of us are wearing  masks and face id just doesn't work with  them  when you're not wearing a mask though it  is amazing in my opinion much better  than touch id  and apple does also say it's much more  secure it also allows for portrait mode  shots using the front camera which look  really good especially if you have  distracting backgrounds you want to hide  let's jump into cameras and this year is  an excellent time to upgrade  the front camera and rear wide and ultra  cameras are the same exact ones in the  pro  you're just missing out on the telephoto  camera which improves the quality of  zoom shots  and lets you take longer portrait mode  shots unless you have a phone from last  year you most likely won't have this  ultra wide and i have to say it is  really nice to have  allowing you to capture shots you  wouldn't have been able to i  loved mine last year but i was always  disappointed with the quality  and thankfully apple has made every shot  much sharper  the biggest upgrade though over last  year's and previous iphones are  nighttime shots where we can now take  night mode shots with all three  cameras now this requires you to hold  your phone for a couple of seconds  and then the a14 processor combines  multiple photos to make them brighter  and sharper  the difference is incredible and it not  only makes  dull dark photos great but allows you to  take photos you otherwise  couldn't now along with that the regular  rear camera takes portrait shots of  people in  objects which adds blur to the  background like pro cameras  for anybody upgrading from a couple year  old iphone or older  the camera difference will be noticeable  especially at night  this also goes for video where for the  first time ever iphones can shoot  hdr which records video more true to  life that's brighter and more colorful  overall i have to say that the iphone 12  is the most complete iphone i've ever  used  and if you've been waiting to upgrade  now is the time it will be great today  and even a few years down the line  thanks to its massive jump in chipsets  and the new design i have very few  complaints this year  i guess one is that the iphone 12 no  longer comes with a power adapter  only a usb type-c charging cable which  won't work with your old five one  adapter  i would suggest buying anker's nano fast  charger for only 16 bucks  which is much smaller than apples and it  will charge your phone  really fast of course you could also buy  apple's magsafe charger but you'll still  need to buy a power brick  the other downside is that the price  went up by a hundred dollars compared to  last year  and maybe even thirty 30 more depending  on which model you want to buy  but i can't really blame them because  the iphone 12 costs apple  much more to build compared to last  year's iphone 11. if i had to boil it  down to one  issue it would be that after you upgrade  to 128 gigs of storage  which i would suggest the price is so  close to the pro model  that it makes it a really tough choice  if you want to see my full comparison  after one week of use to help you decide  which one you should buy  click that video right over there and if  you enjoy this video why not subscribe  by clicking the circle above  let me know your thoughts down in the  comment section below thank you guys for  watching this has been max and i will  see you  in the next video  [Music]  you

